"Wanna express myself to you now,\nFor the lies I've been telling to you.\n\nWanna confess everything now,\nFor the goodbyes I've been telling to you.\n\nI accept your importance yet I see you as distraction,\nI acknowledge your contribution yet I see you as an option.\n\nYou're a part of— no,\nYou are me as we speak till eternity,\nI am you and this cannot be hidden anymore.\n\nWant to apologize for suppressing you for so long,\nBut cannot accept you if I want to go along.\n\nYou might ask, go along with whom?\nYou might ask, why abandon me now?\nYou might ask, why punish me, and you?\n\nAs I speak to you this time,\nChange is universal and cannot be denied.\nI must accept it no matter how harsh it is,\nI must forgive, and forget you to move ahed.\nI mustn't carry you on my shoulders or else,\nI'll lag behind someone who's waiting for me to pass the relay.\nLike you passed me, and now I must keep going.\nLike you abandoned someone too, I must leave you here.\nYou're a dead weight now, we both must accept it.\n\nYou might ask, am I really a dead weight?\nOr are you just denying the fact?\nDenying to experience the free trial of peace,\nAnd then beg for others to buy it for you?\n\nI don't know now,\nFor your points are valid.\nI can't help but, get the anxious trial,\nFor the rhymes I've been killing this time,\nThe expressions are much clearer.\nFor the times I've punished ourselves,\nYet cannot race back now.\nWe must move forward, perhaps just I.\n\nOr shall I just wait here and think?\nIf there is really a competition to compete?"